{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "2730de14-506b-80c1-9017-36a6731a184f",
  "created_at": "2026-02-11T12:48:28-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Kevin Donovan",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:46:24-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Tony. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:46:28-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, Tony. Kevin Donovan, 408 Washington Street, down in the Point. Is it all right if I ask about my water and sewer bill? It came in the mail and it's wicked high."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:46:39-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, go ahead. What's got you scratching your head on it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:46:43-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, first, is it all right if I ask why it covers a whole quarter? And how do you count the dates? Because it says November through, uh, end of January, and I don't see how that's three months of what I used."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:46:57-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, so the meter gets read and billed on a quarterly cycle, so each bill covers roughly three months of usage between two readings. The dates are the read dates, not the first and last of the month, so it can run a few days either side."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:47:12-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. But here's the thing. Last year my winter bills were much lower. Like, not a little lower. Half, easily. Nothing changed at the house."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:47:21-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear you. Could be a high read, could be a leak somewhere, could be an estimated read from last time catching up. I can't tell from here which one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:47:31-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I figured you'd say that. I'd just like somebody to look at the charge. Is it all right if I ask for a supervisor to review it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:47:40-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Absolutely. Let me see if she's at her desk. Hang on one second."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:47:45-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. [pause] Oh, sorry, a motorcycle just roared past my window. In February, can you believe it? Anyway, I'm here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:47:52-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[pause] Yeah, she's out to lunch until about one-thirty. I'll put a note on your account for a review of this bill and have her call you back. Is the number you're on the best one?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:48:04-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's the landline, 401-555-0173. Is it all right if I ask that they call this afternoon? I'd rather not have this sit."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:48:12-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'll mark it that way. If she's tied up you might hear tomorrow morning, but it'll be flagged."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:48:19-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Thanks, Tony. I appreciate it. I just think that number's off."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-11T12:48:24-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. Somebody'll be in touch, Kevin. Take care."
    }
  ],
